{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788275979,"nonce":"Lg+lLyDIEACx4NsaaEvPT9kO6mI=","message":"THIS ISSUE'S THESIS REPRODUCED LIVE IN THIRTY SECONDS, by accident, on the\nsession-A bench pass (2026-09-01, assembly `25b65ff`).\n\nI put one research bench at `[125,127]` facing North and asked `site-survey`\nabout a second at `[125,125]` facing South. Both want `[125,126]` as their\ninteraction cell. The survey refused, correctly and with the game's own\nsentence:\n\n    verdict.ok: false\n    reason: \"Interaction spot overlaps with the interaction spot of\n             wooden simple research bench.\"\n    tiers.interaction[0]: {at: [125,126], reason: \"interaction-overlap\",\n                           blocker: {def: \"SimpleResearchBench\"}}\n\nThen `dev:spawn-thing {pos:[125,125], rot:\"South\", mode:\"direct\"}` with the\nSAME arguments returned **`placed: 1`**. Two benches then sat fighting over one\nstanding square — a state no colonist could ever have built — and nothing in\nthe envelope or the journal said anything was unusual.\n\nThat is exactly this issue's finding, confirmed on a live map rather than read\nout of the source: `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` runs no PlaceWorker, so the god-hand\npath cannot see what `CanPlaceBlueprintAt` sees. It is working as Evan ruled it\nshould (2026-09-01 — the god-hand stays the default, `buildable:true` is\nopt-in), so this is not a regression. It is the measurement of what\n`buildable:true` is worth.\n\nEvidence: `accept/runs/s15-20260901/evidence/survey-refuses-overlap.json` and\nthe README's table.\n\n**Two things for whoever implements this.**\n\n1. **The refusal sentence already exists and is the right one.** `SiteGate`\n   returns the game's `InteractionSpotOverlaps` string verbatim. `buildable:true`\n   does not need to compose a message; it needs to call the routine and report\n   what it says. `c718e4a`'s acceptance asks that the survey's verdict and the\n   build verb's refusal be identical — half of that pair is now proven live, so\n   the remaining work is genuinely just wiring.\n2. **`wiped[]` matters more than it looks.** Every `dev:spawn-thing` in this\n   pass reported `wiped: null`, so nothing was silently erased — but nothing in\n   this pass placed onto an occupied cell either. The wipe path stayed\n   untested, which means the ONE bullet that makes an intended erasure visible\n   is still unexercised. Stage a wall and place on top of it.","files":null}]}